The eStreamer client is written from the protocol as documented in Cisco's
public "Secure Firewall Management Center eStreamer Integration Guide". The
add-on contains no Cisco code.

Output field names are kept the same as earlier versions of this add-on,
which decoded with Cisco's eNcore client library, so existing searches keep
working. They therefore follow that library's output names and spellings
(for example qoa_rule_id).

In bin/fmc_estreamer_tables.py, the IP protocol and TLS cipher suite names
are from the IANA registries. The SSL action, flow status, certificate
status, flow flag, flow message and rule reason names are from the code
tables in Cisco's eStreamer Integration Guide.
